title: Labor Affairs
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: labor_affairs_timer = 6; month_actions += 1;
view-if: ddp_in_government = 1 and labor_minister_party = "DDP" and labor_affairs_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/ErkelenzAnton.png


= Labor Affairs

With our control of the Labor ministry, Anton Erkelenz can finally use his position to advance our agenda of fusing liberalism and organized labor.

- @liberal_unions: Promote the liberal unions.
- @cultivation_consensus: Begin the cultivation of a common consensus between employers and trade unions.
- @increase_welfare: Strengthen social welfare.
- @fund_cooperative_welfare: Strengthen social welfare.
- @decrease_welfare: Cut Welfare.
- @welfare_reforms: Social welfare reforms.
- @continue_reforms: Continue welfare reform.
- @easy_discard

@liberal_unions
on-arrival: workers_ddp += 1; linksliberale_strength += 2; worker_campaign_modifier += 1 if not liberal_unions_promoted; liberal_unions_promoted = 1

Erkelenz has as expectedly led the ministry to become increasingly more friendly with the GdAAB unions by elavating them into the preferred partners in labor-capital negotiations, at the expense of the Free unions and Christian unions and by promote white-collar unionism.

@cultivation_consensus
on-arrival: workers_ddp += 0.5; old_middle_ddp += 0.5; new_middle_ddp += 0.5; capital_strike_progress -= 0.5 if capital_strike_progress > 5; general_strike_progress -= 0.5 if general_strike_progress > 5; labor_consensus_count += 1;

Erkelenz has started to bring buisness leaders and leading unionists together on the synthesis of more comprehensive agreements on labor relations, social policies and others.

@increase_welfare
view-if: labor_welfare_reform_step < 4
choose-if: budget >= 1
subtitle: -1 Budget
unavailable-subtitle: We need 1 budget to expand welfare benefits.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; welfare += 1; workers_ddp += 2

Erkelenz has started to work with other ministries to expands the duration and coverage of welfare benefits for the lower class.

@fund_cooperative_welfare
view-if: labor_welfare_reform_step = 4
choose-if: budget >= 1 and labor_coop_funding < 3
subtitle: -1 Budget
unavailable-subtitle: [? if labor_coop_funding >= 3: It requires no more additional funding to function properly. ?] [? if labor_coop_funding < 3 and budget < 1: We need 1 budget to fund the cooperatives. ?]
on-arrival: budget -= 1; labor_coop_funding += 1; workers_ddp += 2 if labor_coop_funding < 3; workers_ddp += 5 if labor_coop_funding = 3; labor_coop_cap_bonus = 5 if labor_coop_funding = 3

[? if labor_coop_funding < 3: We have allocated more resources to our new coorperative welfare system, and our worker's voters are pleased. ?]

[? if labor_coop_funding = 3: The self-administrated coorperatives is now completely self-sufficient, a great achievement for our party and people of Germany. ?]

@decrease_welfare
subtitle: Whether it is for fiscal discipline or due to urgent need for funding, we have no choice but to cut social welfare. +1 budget
choose-if: welfare >= -5
unavailable-subtitle: There is no more welfare spending to cut.
on-arrival: budget += 1; welfare -= 1; workers_ddp -= 2; unemployed_ddp -= 1; old_middle_ddp += 0.5; new_middle_ddp += 0.5; dvp_relation += 2; spd_relation -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1 if spd_in_government; inflation -= 0.1; economic_growth -= 0.05; unemployed += 0.05; labor_welfare_cut_cap_bonus = 1

Our middle class voters are pleased to see we are cutting 'excess spending', whilst our lower class voters are outraged, have we really chose the correct choice?

@welfare_reforms
view-if: labor_welfare_reform_step = 0 and (labor_progressive_programme = 1 or historical_programme = 1)
subtitle: The current welfare system is a mere contiuation of the Bismarckian system, which should be dismentled and replaced by local cooperatives under the principle of self-help.
choose-if: (economic_minister_party = "DDP" or finance_minister_party = "DDP") and labor_consensus_count >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: [? if economic_minister_party != "DDP" and finance_minister_party != "DDP": We must control either the Ministry of Economics or the Ministry of Finance. ?] [? if labor_consensus_count < 3: There isn't a strong censensus between employers and employees for the social welfare to be distributed while being self-administrated. ?]
on-arrival: workers_ddp += 1; labor_welfare_reform_step = 1;

We have started to create local coorperatives in the hopes of allowing them to distribute social welfare while being self-administrated with the federal government offering technical oversight and limited financial support.

@continue_reforms
subtitle: We have continued to aid local coorperatives and started to allow them to distribute social welfare while being self-administrated with the federal government offering technical oversight and limited financial support.
view-if: labor_welfare_reform_step >= 1 and labor_welfare_reform_step < 4
on-arrival: labor_welfare_reform_step += 1; workers_ddp += 1 if labor_welfare_reform_step < 4; workers_ddp += 2 if labor_welfare_reform_step = 4

[? if labor_welfare_reform_step < 4: We have continued to aid local cooperatives. Their members have begun administering welfare benefits themselves, with the federal government providing technical oversight and limited financial support. ?]

[? if labor_welfare_reform_step = 4: Our long-time effort has born fruit: our new welfare system has replaced the inherently authortarian and statist Bismarckian model.<br>Now we shall continue its funding until it has reached the capacity to be self-sufficient. ?]

# labor_consensus_count : How many consensus action clicked
# labor_welfare_reform_step : Total reform actions, including the initial reform (0 to 4)
# labor_coop_funding : How many clicked increase_welfare button after reform was finished
# labor_welfare_cut_cap_bonus : If welfare cut, worker's vote cap increase
# labor_coop_cap_bonus : If welfare reform is finally done, vote cap greatly increase
